{"type":"delta","text":"This is a genuinely good problem to have — pilot evidence with clinician "}
{"type":"delta","text":"adoption, real opt-out signal, and three legitimate institutional checks all "}
{"type":"delta","text":"arriving at the same time. Let me give you my read on what to fund, in what "}
{"type":"delta","text":"sequence, and how to structure the proof. First, the 40% opt-out rate is not a "}
{"type":"delta","text":"failure signal — it's a segmentation signal. In ambient documentation pilots "}
{"type":"delta","text":"I've seen across integrated health systems, opt-out rates in that range almost "}
{"type":"delta","text":"always cluster around two causes: specialty-specific workflow fit (the tool was "}
{"type":"delta","text":"trained on note patterns that don't match how that specialty actually documents) "}
{"type":"delta","text":"and change-management gaps (insufficient training, no peer champion, no feedback "}
{"type":"delta","text":"loop for clinicians to flag inaccuracies). Your CMIO's instinct to push forward "}
{"type":"delta","text":"is right, but a direct 23-specialty rollout without diagnosing those two causes "}
{"type":"delta","text":"will embed the 40% resistance pattern system-wide. That's the failure mode to "}
{"type":"delta","text":"avoid. What I'd fund in sequence: Phase one — before rollout, run a short "}
{"type":"delta","text":"diagnostic sprint (six to eight weeks) across your two pilot specialties. "}
{"type":"delta","text":"Identify what specifically drove opt-out: is it note structure mismatch, "}
{"type":"delta","text":"latency, EHR integration friction, or trust gaps in accuracy? This is not "}
{"type":"delta","text":"expensive — it's structured interviews and structured review of notes flagged as "}
{"type":"delta","text":"requiring heavy editing. The output is a segmentation of your 23 specialties "}
{"type":"delta","text":"into high-fit, medium-fit, and adaptation-required cohorts."}
{"type":"followups","followups":["Of the 40% opt-out rate, how do we quickly distinguish between fixable workflow/training issues versus specialties where ambient documentation is genuinely a poor fit? What's the fastest way to run that diagnostic sprint without delaying the rollout timeline the CMIO is pushing?","For the FDA AI-SaMD and HIPAA compliance gates: should we treat those as pre-rollout blockers that need resolution before Phase Two, or can we structure them as parallel workstreams while we validate clinical fit? What's the minimum viable governance posture our CISO and compliance team need to see before we expand beyond cardiology and orthopedics?","The CFO will ask 'what's the unit economics and where's the realized value?' — should we define that as clinician time recovered per note, reduction in documentation errors caught downstream, or revenue cycle acceleration? How do we pilot the measurement framework in these two specialties so we have credible numbers for the 23-specialty business case?"]}
{"type":"done"}

