{"type":"delta","text":"The active tenant in my connected data is Apex Retail — not a health system. So "}
{"type":"delta","text":"I don't have an Epic deployment, clinical AI substrate, ambient documentation "}
{"type":"delta","text":"pilot, or research AI direction to draw on, because none of those exist in your "}
{"type":"delta","text":"enterprise layer.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"If you're asking me to reason about those topics in the abstract — Epic's AI "}
{"type":"delta","text":"strategy, ambient documentation pilots in health systems, clinical AI substrate "}
{"type":"delta","text":"patterns — I can do that, but I'd want to flag it's general industry knowledge, "}
{"type":"delta","text":"not anything specific to your organization.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"More likely, you may be thinking of a different AbarVa tenant, or there's a "}
{"type":"delta","text":"mismatch in how the session was initialized. Worth checking that before we go "}
{"type":"delta","text":"further — I'd rather tell you that cleanly than fabricate a clinical context "}
{"type":"delta","text":"that isn't yours.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"What would be most useful from here?"}
{"type":"followups","followups":["Which AbarVa tenant should I actually be connected to for this conversation — is there a different environment or workspace I need to switch to in order to access the health system deployment data?","If I do have access to clinical AI substrate or ambient documentation pilot data elsewhere in our infrastructure, how would I verify which tenant it's associated with and ensure I'm pulling from the right connected data source?","Can you walk me through what the correct session initialization should look like for health system use cases, so I can understand whether this is a configuration issue on my end or a gap in how the Apex Retail tenant was set up?"]}
