{"type":"delta","text":"I don't have your pilot measurement data in the connected tenant layer — what's "}
{"type":"delta","text":"actually been recorded for your Abridge deployment isn't surfacing here, so I "}
{"type":"delta","text":"can't give you a number from your own program.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"What I can tell you is how to pressure-test the 50% claim. That figure comes "}
{"type":"delta","text":"from Abridge's own studies, typically measuring time-in-documentation against a "}
{"type":"delta","text":"pre-implementation baseline in controlled conditions. Real-world enterprise "}
{"type":"delta","text":"pilots consistently land lower — the pattern I've seen puts realized savings "}
{"type":"delta","text":"closer to 20-35% when you control for physician adoption variance, note review "}
{"type":"delta","text":"and editing behavior, and how documentation time was originally measured.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"The critical question isn't time saved in the tool — it's whether that time "}
{"type":"delta","text":"translated into something measurable on your P&L or capacity utilization. Did "}
{"type":"delta","text":"saved documentation time reduce overtime, increase patient throughput, or show "}
{"type":"delta","text":"up in physician satisfaction scores? If your pilot didn't instrument those "}
{"type":"delta","text":"downstream outcomes, the 50% figure is activity measurement, not value "}
{"type":"delta","text":"measurement.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"For your actual pilot data — utilization rates, note completion times, adoption "}
{"type":"delta","text":"by role — your clinical informatics or AI platform team would have it. That's "}
{"type":"delta","text":"the right conversation to have before you make a scale decision."}
{"type":"followups","followups":["How should we instrument our pilot to capture downstream outcomes like overtime reduction or throughput gains, rather than just activity metrics?","Who owns the pilot measurement data in our organization, and what specific utilization and adoption metrics should we be requesting from them right now?","If our realized savings land at 20-35%, what adoption or usage threshold would we need to hit to justify the Abridge investment against our current documentation costs?"]}
{"type":"done"}

