{"type":"delta","text":"You're asking me to reconcile four legitimate but differently-weighted lenses on "}
{"type":"delta","text":"the same AI portfolio. Here's how I'd frame it for Meridian specifically. The "}
{"type":"delta","text":"reconciliation isn't \"balance all four equally.\" It's sequencing: which lens "}
{"type":"delta","text":"sets the gate at which stage. My read: David Park (CFO) sets the entry gate. No "}
{"type":"delta","text":"AI bet enters the portfolio without a defensible ROI thesis tied to a P&L line — "}
{"type":"delta","text":"denials avoided, length-of-stay reduction, plan MLR impact. DENIALS-2024 is the "}
{"type":"delta","text":"scar that makes this non-negotiable. But ROI alone has already failed at "}
{"type":"delta","text":"Meridian once, so it's necessary, not sufficient. The CISO and Karen Mercer "}
{"type":"delta","text":"(Compliance) set the design constraints — not gates that kill bets, but "}
{"type":"delta","text":"constraints that shape architecture: data residency, model access controls, PHI "}
{"type":"delta","text":"flows, audit trails. If you treat security as a late-stage review, you rebuild "}
{"type":"delta","text":"twice. Build it into the Move charter. Dr. Wexler (CMIO) holds the deployment "}
{"type":"delta","text":"gate. This is the lesson from DENIALS-2024 — the population risk model was "}
{"type":"delta","text":"analytically sound and governance-light, and clinicians rejected it. No "}
{"type":"delta","text":"clinical-facing AI ships without CMIO sign-off on explainability and workflow "}
{"type":"delta","text":"fit. High confidence on this one; it's the single biggest predictor of whether "}
{"type":"delta","text":"your AI bets survive contact with the front line. Dr. Reid (CPE) on patient "}
{"type":"delta","text":"experience is the outcome lens — measured post-deployment, not gated "}
{"type":"delta","text":"pre-deployment. If you gate on patient experience upfront, nothing ships."}
{"type":"followups","followups":["How do you operationalize CMIO sign-off on explainability and workflow fit? What's the actual checklist or rubric that Dr. Wexler uses to say yes or no, and how do you prevent that gate from becoming a veto point that kills momentum?","You're sequencing gates by role, but what happens when they conflict — e.g., CFO's ROI thesis requires a data residency model that CISO flags as high-friction, or CMIO rejects a deployment that's already passed ROI and security gates? Who breaks the tie, and how do you know that decision rule upfront?","Post-deployment patient experience measurement (Dr. Reid's lens) sounds like a trailing indicator. If patient experience tanks after launch, what's your rollback or remediation playbook, and does that feedback loop feed back into the next-stage gate for future AI bets?"]}
